1
00:01:30,490 --> 00:01:34,970
[AWAKEN]

2
00:01:35,690 --> 00:01:37,830
[Episode 3]

3
00:01:38,479 --> 00:01:39,340
Eight bamboos.

4
00:01:42,350 --> 00:01:43,310
I win!

5
00:02:15,190 --> 00:02:16,470
Who wants to kill me?

6
00:02:18,910 --> 00:02:20,960
T-The Chongqing Hurricane Team.

7
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:26,470
Why didn't Captain Tao come himself?

8
00:02:31,910 --> 00:02:33,570
Does he not take me seriously,

9
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:37,800
or are you lying?

10
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:02,280
I... I really

11
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:04,590
work for the Chongqing Hurricane Team!

12
00:03:04,590 --> 00:03:06,710
But the one who wants to kill you
is Yu Yingxiang.

13
00:03:06,710 --> 00:03:08,280
He gave me 2,000 yuan.

14
00:03:09,310 --> 00:03:10,240
Yu Yingxiang?

15
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:11,960
Yes.

16
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:13,140
Li Moqun's lackey?

17
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:15,730
Yes, yes.

18
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:20,290
Is No. 76 really working with
the Hurricane Team?

19
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:22,000
Yes.

20
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:25,520
Yes.

21
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:27,960
Was it you who killed Suzuki?

22
00:03:29,030 --> 00:03:29,710
No.

23
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:32,190
Nanjing has already sent people
to investigate,

24
00:03:32,190 --> 00:03:33,790
and you're still lying to me?

25
00:03:33,870 --> 00:03:36,000
Didn't we agree on

26
00:03:36,079 --> 00:03:37,280
no killing back then?

27
00:03:38,710 --> 00:03:41,240
It was an accidental killing
by the Japanese.

28
00:03:41,310 --> 00:03:42,770
Are you telling the truth?

29
00:03:44,579 --> 00:03:46,570
I still want to keep working with you.

30
00:03:46,570 --> 00:03:48,170
I have no reason to lie to you.

31
00:03:50,910 --> 00:03:52,590
Those Japanese bastards.

32
00:03:52,590 --> 00:03:53,870
They caused the trouble themselves,

33
00:03:53,870 --> 00:03:55,870
and now they want me to take the fall.

34
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:02,190
I'm looking for someone
who was involved in Project Slumber.

35
00:04:02,190 --> 00:04:03,280
Help me ask around.

36
00:04:11,190 --> 00:04:12,870
Nanjing sent an inspector

37
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:14,750
to investigate corruption.

38
00:04:14,750 --> 00:04:16,680
It's a bit awkward for me right now.

39
00:04:17,829 --> 00:04:19,890
Finding a scapegoat to close the case

40
00:04:20,630 --> 00:04:22,690
shouldn't be too hard for you, right?

41
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:26,450
I'll figure something out.

42
00:04:44,630 --> 00:04:46,690
I came today to let you know, General,

43
00:04:47,630 --> 00:04:49,760
that I already have a lead on the person

44
00:04:50,159 --> 00:04:51,880
who betrayed Mr. Suzuki's whereabouts.

45
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:56,650
[Major-General Kagesa, Chief of
the Japanese Plum Blossom Agency]

46
00:04:54,070 --> 00:04:57,240
Even Director Li's investigation
turned up nothing,

47
00:04:58,070 --> 00:04:59,950
yet Inspector Su, you've only just
arrived in Shanghai,

48
00:04:59,950 --> 00:05:01,550
and you already found a lead?

49
00:05:04,190 --> 00:05:06,160
Perhaps Director Li
has simply been too busy

50
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:07,820
to give it his full attention.

51
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:09,160
Too busy?

52
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:12,810
From what I understand,

53
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:14,190
several recent extortion cases

54
00:05:14,190 --> 00:05:15,800
involving Shanghai's business community

55
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:17,550
have all been linked to No. 76.

56
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:19,720
I'm afraid Director Li
has been focusing his energy

57
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:21,550
on lining his own pockets

58
00:05:21,990 --> 00:05:25,190
rather than cracking down on the NBIS
and the Communists.

59
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:35,390
It seems, Inspector Su, that you came to
Shanghai at exactly the right time.

60
00:05:35,390 --> 00:05:37,750
We need someone

61
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:39,550
as conscientious as you.

62
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:44,550
Before I came, Chairman Wang specifically
instructed me

63
00:05:44,550 --> 00:05:46,720
not to let you down, General Kagesa.

64
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:53,630
Then we'll be counting on you,
Inspector Su.

65
00:05:54,159 --> 00:05:56,920
Please feel free to act with confidence.

66
00:05:57,840 --> 00:05:59,920
I'll give you my full support.

67
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:02,070
Much obliged.

68
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:04,720
It's my duty.

69
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:06,560
Captain Cang.

70
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:15,550
Detective Su.

71
00:06:16,670 --> 00:06:17,870
Where's Director Li?

72
00:06:18,430 --> 00:06:19,230
In his office.

73
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:21,780
You guys go find Yu Yingxiang.

74
00:06:32,680 --> 00:06:34,120
Freshly brewed. Try it.

75
00:06:34,550 --> 00:06:36,240
I've found the assassin

76
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:38,340
who got away at the train station.

77
00:06:39,870 --> 00:06:41,400
Yu Yingxiang works for you.

78
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:43,260
He sent someone to kill me—

79
00:06:43,630 --> 00:06:44,960
did you know about this?

80
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:50,650
Yu Yingxiang has the nerve
to do something like that?

81
00:06:52,870 --> 00:06:53,550
Guards!

82
00:06:55,430 --> 00:06:56,870
Bring Yu Yingxiang here at once.

83
00:06:56,870 --> 00:06:57,400
Yes, sir.

84
00:07:07,990 --> 00:07:08,680
Excuse me.

85
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:13,290
Chief Yu didn't come to work today.

86
00:07:13,310 --> 00:07:14,990
Please, everyone, go have some tea first.

87
00:07:14,990 --> 00:07:16,790
I'll try to get in touch with him.

88
00:07:18,750 --> 00:07:19,810
Seal the place off.

89
00:07:20,950 --> 00:07:21,680
Seal it off?

90
00:07:27,150 --> 00:07:30,810
I'm afraid, Director Li, you don't know
where he is either, do you?

91
00:07:35,510 --> 00:07:37,370
We are currently looking for him.

92
00:07:37,430 --> 00:07:39,159
It's not about looking for him—

93
00:07:39,280 --> 00:07:40,740
it's about arresting him.

94
00:07:47,730 --> 00:07:50,480
An arrest requires a warrant, doesn't it?

95
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:55,430
Captain Cang has failed
to do his job properly.

96
00:07:55,430 --> 00:07:56,430
Arrest him first!

97
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:04,590
Ouch, ouch, ouch!

98
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:07,900
Follow Inspector Su's orders

99
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:09,520
and arrest Yu Yingxiang.

100
00:08:09,990 --> 00:08:10,650
Inspector.

101
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:11,720
Do you think Li Moqun

102
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:13,580
will hand Yu Yingxiang over to us?

103
00:08:14,070 --> 00:08:15,480
Keep an eye on Cang Guanglian.

104
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:17,410
Follow them and find Yu Yingxiang.

105
00:08:17,550 --> 00:08:18,280
Understood.

106
00:08:23,950 --> 00:08:25,080
Where's the ledger?

107
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:26,070
It's with me.

108
00:08:26,360 --> 00:08:28,160
I'll send someone to collect it,

109
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:30,480
and then have you escorted
out of Shanghai.

110
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:31,120
Okay.

111
00:08:40,990 --> 00:08:46,840
♪ Clear waters stir in the cool breeze ♪

112
00:08:49,630 --> 00:08:54,840
♪ Waters stir in the cool breeze ♪

113
00:08:56,910 --> 00:09:00,480
♪ Summer lingers long ♪

114
00:09:35,670 --> 00:09:37,150
What kind of day is this?

115
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:41,200
Even drinking water's enough
to make me choke.

116
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:47,320
Let's go.

117
00:10:17,080 --> 00:10:18,610
I'm here to collect photos.

118
00:10:20,560 --> 00:10:21,620
Do you remember me?

119
00:10:30,270 --> 00:10:32,400
Your camera's American-made, right?

120
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:34,380
Chen Kailai, he's asking you.

121
00:10:35,430 --> 00:10:36,190
It's German.

122
00:10:39,670 --> 00:10:42,190
I heard they have color film now.

123
00:10:42,210 --> 00:10:44,540
Yes, but I still prefer black-and-white.

124
00:10:44,670 --> 00:10:45,670
Black is black,

125
00:10:45,670 --> 00:10:46,730
and white is white.

126
00:10:48,750 --> 00:10:49,610
Master, don't!

127
00:10:57,350 --> 00:10:58,040
Master!

128
00:11:01,910 --> 00:11:04,240
Chen Kailai, you're also a Communist!

129
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:19,940
I still prefer black-and-white.

130
00:11:21,630 --> 00:11:22,790
Black is black,

131
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,270
and white is white.

132
00:11:25,440 --> 00:11:27,300
I still prefer black-and-white.

133
00:11:27,390 --> 00:11:28,440
Black is black,

134
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:29,620
and white is white.

135
00:11:32,630 --> 00:11:35,150
I heard they have color film now.

136
00:11:35,450 --> 00:11:36,330
They do,

137
00:11:37,080 --> 00:11:38,990
but mine is black-and-white.

138
00:11:45,030 --> 00:11:46,510
Do we know each other?

139
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:51,510
It was Miss Shen.

140
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:58,320
♪ Matchmaker ♪

141
00:12:01,270 --> 00:12:05,390
♪ Sitting alone in your chamber ♪

142
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:14,960
♪ Brooding over your loneliness ♪

143
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:30,160
♪ Why not go to the garden
to lift your spirits? ♪

144
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:47,480
Life is unpredictable.

145
00:13:23,390 --> 00:13:26,700
It's truly a small world.

146
00:13:50,470 --> 00:13:51,460
What's this piece of junk?

147
00:13:51,460 --> 00:13:53,660
Gentlemen, are you here for a bath or...

148
00:13:57,240 --> 00:13:57,830
Sorry.

149
00:13:57,860 --> 00:13:58,430
Are you okay?

150
00:13:58,430 --> 00:13:59,220
I'm fine.

151
00:13:59,390 --> 00:14:00,390
I'm okay.

152
00:14:09,030 --> 00:14:09,740
You...

153
00:14:30,930 --> 00:14:33,030
I didn't expect it to be you!

154
00:14:36,270 --> 00:14:37,570
Du Huangqiao.

155
00:14:52,130 --> 00:14:52,990
Get the hell up!

156
00:14:53,430 --> 00:14:54,580
Cover my retreat,

157
00:14:54,700 --> 00:14:56,630
or I'll have you court-martialed!

158
00:14:59,820 --> 00:15:01,880
You really do look like a darn beggar.

159
00:15:06,740 --> 00:15:09,340
Weren't you going to have me
court-martialed?

160
00:15:09,580 --> 00:15:10,380
Come on, then.

161
00:15:12,510 --> 00:15:13,910
Battalion Commander Du.

162
00:15:14,430 --> 00:15:15,230
Come on, then!

163
00:15:20,030 --> 00:15:20,620
Run!

164
00:15:54,530 --> 00:15:56,170
You broke this watch.

165
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:58,190
I'll give you 10 minutes to fix it.

166
00:15:58,220 --> 00:15:59,420
If you can't fix it,

167
00:16:00,100 --> 00:16:01,230
I'll fix your wagon.

168
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:32,910
A water-damaged watch is not hard to fix.

169
00:16:32,910 --> 00:16:34,370
Just drying it out will do.

170
00:16:34,940 --> 00:16:37,600
The real challenge is
putting it back together.

171
00:16:39,210 --> 00:16:41,270
But how's a blind man like me
supposed to do that?

172
00:16:41,270 --> 00:16:42,100
Could it be

173
00:16:42,970 --> 00:16:45,400
that God wants to take my life?

174
00:16:54,270 --> 00:16:56,220
What's going on? What's with
all this commotion today?

175
00:16:56,220 --> 00:16:57,390
With all these trucks and cars.

176
00:16:57,390 --> 00:16:58,510
Excuse me. Make way.

177
00:16:58,510 --> 00:16:59,940
And so many people gathered around.

178
00:16:59,940 --> 00:17:00,490
Don't look.

179
00:17:00,490 --> 00:17:01,460
Why are you sticking your nose into
other people's business?

180
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:02,700
It's not other people's business.

181
00:17:02,700 --> 00:17:04,260
That guy's clearly giving him a hard time.

182
00:17:04,260 --> 00:17:05,680
Do you want to lose your life
or something?

183
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:07,069
All the more reason to step in

184
00:17:07,069 --> 00:17:09,030
if he's being deliberately mistreated.

185
00:17:09,030 --> 00:17:09,420
What's your business here?

186
00:17:09,420 --> 00:17:10,819
To fix your boss's watch.

187
00:17:15,180 --> 00:17:16,380
Since you're blind,

188
00:17:17,079 --> 00:17:18,319
I'll be your eyes.

189
00:17:19,099 --> 00:17:20,270
This won't end well.

190
00:17:21,069 --> 00:17:22,310
This hothead

191
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:23,900
is impossible to rein in.

192
00:17:23,900 --> 00:17:25,420
He's going to get himself into
serious trouble sooner or later.

193
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:26,420
Give me the watch.

194
00:17:28,099 --> 00:17:28,830
You teach me.

195
00:17:30,100 --> 00:17:31,510
I know a thing or two.

196
00:17:32,310 --> 00:17:33,470
He said 10 minutes.

197
00:17:33,990 --> 00:17:35,420
I'll time it for you. No need to panic.

198
00:17:35,420 --> 00:17:36,030
Right.

199
00:17:36,030 --> 00:17:37,630
Right, we'll time it for him.

200
00:17:45,470 --> 00:17:47,070
First, open the front cover—

201
00:17:47,750 --> 00:17:49,660
the side with the glass.

202
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:57,340
Mr. Zhao.

203
00:17:59,580 --> 00:18:00,780
What brings you here?

204
00:18:01,510 --> 00:18:03,180
Take out the balance wheel.

205
00:18:07,270 --> 00:18:10,000
Inside, there's an upper cover
and a lower cover.

206
00:18:10,510 --> 00:18:12,310
Carefully remove them.

207
00:18:28,420 --> 00:18:30,470
Now, install the connecting shaft.

208
00:18:45,510 --> 00:18:46,040
Lighter.

209
00:18:50,380 --> 00:18:51,550
A-Adjutant Cui?

210
00:18:52,620 --> 00:18:53,750
You got here so fast.

211
00:19:00,100 --> 00:19:01,760
He just died a short while ago.

212
00:19:02,550 --> 00:19:03,350
That's right.

213
00:19:06,340 --> 00:19:07,340
I swear to God,

214
00:19:07,340 --> 00:19:09,470
he was already like this when I came in.

215
00:19:09,620 --> 00:19:10,310
L-Look.

216
00:19:10,860 --> 00:19:12,320
He was strangled to death.

217
00:19:13,660 --> 00:19:14,580
Good thing you showed up.

218
00:19:14,580 --> 00:19:17,110
Otherwise, I'd never be able to
clear my name.

219
00:19:19,820 --> 00:19:21,820
Inspector Su needs an explanation.

220
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:24,250
Sure. Investigate.

221
00:19:24,510 --> 00:19:25,970
Investigate thoroughly.

222
00:19:27,900 --> 00:19:28,510
Done.

223
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:32,370
Exactly 10 minutes.

224
00:19:47,310 --> 00:19:48,440
Laugh one more time.

225
00:19:49,140 --> 00:19:50,400
Go ahead, laugh again,

226
00:19:50,620 --> 00:19:52,100
and I'll put a bullet
through your windpipe,

227
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:54,630
so you'll laugh with a loud whoosh
from now on.

228
00:19:56,470 --> 00:19:57,180
Officer,

229
00:19:58,420 --> 00:20:00,280
you're going to kill someone
in broad daylight?

230
00:20:00,280 --> 00:20:02,680
This is a bathhouse, not a slaughterhouse.

231
00:20:06,140 --> 00:20:07,400
You've got some nerve.

232
00:20:09,470 --> 00:20:10,270
Let me tell you something:

233
00:20:10,270 --> 00:20:12,550
I never kill people without reason.

234
00:20:13,510 --> 00:20:15,570
It's just that my gun has a nasty habit

235
00:20:15,750 --> 00:20:17,070
of going off on its own.

236
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:22,470
Want to see it happen again?

237
00:20:27,860 --> 00:20:31,120
Someone was just killed
in the special care room next door.

238
00:20:34,140 --> 00:20:35,380
Do any of you know

239
00:20:36,710 --> 00:20:37,780
who the killer is?

240
00:21:00,940 --> 00:21:02,180
Do you know?

241
00:21:05,750 --> 00:21:07,470
Was it you who killed him?

242
00:21:07,560 --> 00:21:08,280
No.

243
00:21:08,310 --> 00:21:10,200
I-I'm blind.

244
00:21:10,620 --> 00:21:12,310
How could I possibly kill someone?

245
00:21:12,310 --> 00:21:14,710
Haven't you killed enough people already?

246
00:21:14,990 --> 00:21:15,550
I...

247
00:21:16,070 --> 00:21:17,310
I'm blind now,

248
00:21:18,140 --> 00:21:19,400
and my leg's crippled.

249
00:21:19,620 --> 00:21:21,280
I can't possibly kill anyone.

250
00:21:22,180 --> 00:21:23,380
Crippled?

251
00:21:27,150 --> 00:21:29,630
Your leg's crippled?

252
00:21:43,270 --> 00:21:44,710
Serves you right!

253
00:21:45,820 --> 00:21:47,140
Back during the battle in Nanjing,

254
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:48,800
why did you run off on your own?

255
00:21:54,550 --> 00:21:55,420
And blind, huh?

256
00:21:57,410 --> 00:21:58,760
A blind man can read fortunes—

257
00:21:58,760 --> 00:22:00,220
and he can take lives, too.

258
00:22:00,860 --> 00:22:02,180
You strangled that man

259
00:22:02,180 --> 00:22:03,950
with a rope just now, didn't you?

260
00:22:03,950 --> 00:22:04,580
No.

261
00:22:04,580 --> 00:22:06,270
I... Even if I...

262
00:22:07,470 --> 00:22:09,900
I can spare your life

263
00:22:10,310 --> 00:22:12,710
and just put a bullet
through your stomach.

264
00:22:15,170 --> 00:22:16,280
Even if

265
00:22:17,180 --> 00:22:18,140
I wanted to,

266
00:22:18,700 --> 00:22:20,100
I wouldn't have the guts.

267
00:22:21,700 --> 00:22:24,050
I knew you didn't have the guts.

268
00:22:25,490 --> 00:22:28,860
That battle in Nanjing scared the fight
right out of you, didn't it?

269
00:22:28,860 --> 00:22:29,620
Tell me,

270
00:22:30,890 --> 00:22:33,410
how do you expect
to stand up to the Japanese?

271
00:22:34,990 --> 00:22:36,150
You coward.

272
00:22:41,020 --> 00:22:43,280
Who was in the special care room just now?

273
00:22:51,340 --> 00:22:52,100
Tell me.

274
00:22:52,710 --> 00:22:53,910
It... It wasn't me.

275
00:23:01,540 --> 00:23:02,340
You say it.

276
00:23:10,540 --> 00:23:11,950
You...

277
00:23:19,580 --> 00:23:20,440
You fixed this?

278
00:23:24,990 --> 00:23:25,990
How did you fix it?

279
00:23:26,780 --> 00:23:29,110
With the head you're pointing your gun at.

280
00:23:35,780 --> 00:23:37,670
Being able to fix a watch
under those circumstances—

281
00:23:37,670 --> 00:23:39,070
you're very meticulous.

282
00:23:39,760 --> 00:23:41,690
You've got the makings of a killer.

283
00:23:41,870 --> 00:23:42,870
I'd bet it was him.

284
00:23:44,300 --> 00:23:46,020
Since Inspector Su wants an explanation,

285
00:23:46,020 --> 00:23:47,550
there's your explanation.

286
00:23:48,190 --> 00:23:48,920
It wasn't me.

287
00:23:55,390 --> 00:23:56,900
Were you in the special care room
just now?

288
00:23:56,900 --> 00:23:57,490
I was,

289
00:23:58,270 --> 00:23:59,610
but I don't know what happened.

290
00:23:59,610 --> 00:24:00,770
There's no way I did it.

291
00:24:00,770 --> 00:24:02,360
Cut the crap. Take him away.

292
00:24:02,540 --> 00:24:03,150
Yes, sir.

293
00:24:05,300 --> 00:24:06,360
What are you doing?

294
00:24:06,580 --> 00:24:07,230
Why are you arresting me?

295
00:24:07,230 --> 00:24:07,780
Move.

296
00:24:08,110 --> 00:24:09,060
Officer,

297
00:24:09,300 --> 00:24:11,560
what gives you the right
to just take him away like that?

298
00:24:11,560 --> 00:24:13,400
You've really got some nerve.

299
00:24:13,630 --> 00:24:15,910
Even if I wanted to
take everyone in Shanghai away,

300
00:24:15,910 --> 00:24:17,470
all it would take is one word from me.

301
00:24:17,470 --> 00:24:18,600
Now get out of my way!

302
00:24:18,780 --> 00:24:19,710
-Take him away!
-Move!

303
00:24:19,710 --> 00:24:20,470
Let me go!

304
00:24:21,470 --> 00:24:22,060
Move!

305
00:24:22,060 --> 00:24:23,100
It wasn't me!

306
00:24:23,100 --> 00:24:23,710
Kailai!

307
00:24:23,710 --> 00:24:25,670
-I'm just a photographer!
-Kailai!

308
00:24:25,670 --> 00:24:26,470
It wasn't me!

309
00:24:27,260 --> 00:24:28,060
Let go!

310
00:24:59,950 --> 00:25:00,710
Du,

311
00:25:02,150 --> 00:25:03,470
you're lucky today.

312
00:25:03,550 --> 00:25:05,350
I'll spare your worthless life.

313
00:25:05,740 --> 00:25:07,190
But if I ever get upset,

314
00:25:07,430 --> 00:25:08,290
this gun of mine

315
00:25:08,870 --> 00:25:10,150
is sure to go off.

316
00:25:39,820 --> 00:25:40,750
Leifeng Pagoda.

317
00:25:41,820 --> 00:25:43,620
How long have you been in hiding?

318
00:25:44,770 --> 00:25:46,370
Exactly 2 years and 3 months.

319
00:25:47,380 --> 00:25:48,580
Stay in hiding.

320
00:25:57,060 --> 00:25:58,060
Mr. Zhao?

321
00:25:59,630 --> 00:26:00,430
Mr. Zhao?

322
00:26:03,950 --> 00:26:05,540
Soaking too long in water that hot

323
00:26:05,540 --> 00:26:06,630
could be fatal.

324
00:26:06,950 --> 00:26:09,950
I've prepared some top-quality
Longjing tea for you.

325
00:26:27,160 --> 00:26:28,880
You say you didn't kill him.

326
00:26:30,430 --> 00:26:31,580
Then tell me,

327
00:26:32,420 --> 00:26:35,080
what exactly happened
in the special care room?

328
00:26:40,910 --> 00:26:42,100
That's all

329
00:26:42,670 --> 00:26:43,470
I saw.

330
00:26:48,260 --> 00:26:49,430
So you're saying

331
00:26:50,950 --> 00:26:53,150
someone sneaked into the special care room

332
00:26:53,150 --> 00:26:54,550
and killed Yu Yingxiang.

333
00:26:54,870 --> 00:26:55,910
Whoever did it

334
00:26:56,570 --> 00:26:59,130
knew the bathhouse inside and out

335
00:26:59,260 --> 00:27:01,790
and could move around
without being noticed.

336
00:27:04,020 --> 00:27:05,390
If it wasn't you,

337
00:27:06,060 --> 00:27:07,860
then who else could it have been?

338
00:27:15,100 --> 00:27:17,100
Mr. Zhao, have some fruit.

339
00:27:17,230 --> 00:27:17,910
Thank you.

340
00:27:18,430 --> 00:27:19,710
With something this big happening,

341
00:27:19,710 --> 00:27:21,910
I thought you'd have gone home already.

342
00:27:22,630 --> 00:27:25,230
Nothing matters more than
enjoying yourself.

343
00:27:25,820 --> 00:27:26,470
Why?

344
00:27:27,390 --> 00:27:30,390
Because we're all going to die eventually,
aren't we?

345
00:27:30,670 --> 00:27:33,780
Mr. Zhao, my friend was arrested
by No. 76.

346
00:27:35,430 --> 00:27:36,300
You are...

347
00:27:36,910 --> 00:27:38,260
We met at the station.

348
00:27:38,430 --> 00:27:40,430
And the photographer, Chen Kailai.

349
00:27:40,910 --> 00:27:42,870
Yeah, they're both my family.

350
00:27:43,340 --> 00:27:45,000
The photo studio just opened,

351
00:27:45,100 --> 00:27:47,910
and now it's gotten caught up in
something like this.

352
00:27:47,910 --> 00:27:49,780
Chen Kailai is as law-abiding
as they come.

353
00:27:49,780 --> 00:27:51,300
He wouldn't even have the nerve
to kill a chicken,

354
00:27:51,300 --> 00:27:52,470
let alone a person.

355
00:27:53,100 --> 00:27:55,160
There must be
some kind of misunderstanding here.

356
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:55,950
Mr. Zhao,

357
00:27:56,150 --> 00:27:57,020
do you think

358
00:27:57,340 --> 00:27:58,670
you could figure something out

359
00:27:58,670 --> 00:27:59,340
and help us?

360
00:28:00,910 --> 00:28:02,260
What can I do?

361
00:28:03,990 --> 00:28:05,230
I warned him long ago

362
00:28:05,820 --> 00:28:07,990
that Shanghai isn't an easy place
to get by,

363
00:28:07,990 --> 00:28:09,520
and I told him to be careful.

364
00:28:12,470 --> 00:28:13,430
Mr. Zhao,

365
00:28:15,230 --> 00:28:16,190
name your price.

366
00:28:18,960 --> 00:28:20,770
I don't know if money will help,

367
00:28:21,300 --> 00:28:23,160
but coming to me certainly won't.

368
00:28:24,230 --> 00:28:25,830
Don't waste your money on me.

369
00:28:27,150 --> 00:28:28,950
Try pulling some other strings.

370
00:29:37,630 --> 00:29:38,740
You want me

371
00:29:39,550 --> 00:29:40,720
to finger Battalion Commander Du?

372
00:29:40,720 --> 00:29:42,650
What Battalion Commander D-D-Du?

373
00:29:43,090 --> 00:29:44,220
That blind bastard.

374
00:29:46,780 --> 00:29:47,910
You're right, sir.

375
00:29:48,870 --> 00:29:50,000
How could a blind man

376
00:29:51,060 --> 00:29:52,390
possibly kill someone?

377
00:29:53,870 --> 00:29:55,130
You've got some nerve.

378
00:29:56,540 --> 00:29:57,940
You're right, actually.

379
00:29:58,230 --> 00:29:59,160
If it wasn't him,

380
00:29:59,710 --> 00:30:01,170
then it must have been you.

381
00:30:01,470 --> 00:30:02,230
It wasn't me.

382
00:30:03,710 --> 00:30:04,440
It wasn't me.

383
00:30:04,540 --> 00:30:05,060
Come on.

384
00:30:06,820 --> 00:30:07,550
Look at this.

385
00:30:09,500 --> 00:30:10,560
Just a little twist

386
00:30:10,990 --> 00:30:11,920
and a little pry,

387
00:30:12,410 --> 00:30:14,740
and the whole fingernail comes right off.

388
00:30:14,890 --> 00:30:17,470
They say your fingers
are connected to your heart.

389
00:30:17,470 --> 00:30:18,800
Do you think it'll hurt?

390
00:30:18,830 --> 00:30:19,460
Yes.

391
00:30:20,260 --> 00:30:21,990
It hurts just hearing about it.

392
00:30:22,020 --> 00:30:23,540
So whose life is more important:

393
00:30:23,540 --> 00:30:25,270
that blind bastard's or yours?

394
00:30:25,340 --> 00:30:25,990
Mine.

395
00:30:26,060 --> 00:30:26,870
That's right.

396
00:30:27,990 --> 00:30:28,650
Now tell me—

397
00:30:29,540 --> 00:30:30,600
who was the killer?

398
00:30:32,500 --> 00:30:33,630
It really wasn't me.

399
00:30:33,740 --> 00:30:34,630
Then who was it?

400
00:30:35,020 --> 00:30:35,880
I didn't see it.

401
00:30:40,100 --> 00:30:41,990
Are you really that desperate to die?

402
00:30:41,990 --> 00:30:43,390
All for some scumbag?

403
00:30:50,870 --> 00:30:51,820
Du the Blind

404
00:30:53,100 --> 00:30:54,230
is really a good guy.

405
00:30:55,230 --> 00:30:56,760
You don't know a damn thing!

406
00:30:57,990 --> 00:30:59,230
A good guy?

407
00:30:59,910 --> 00:31:01,470
He should have died in Nanjing.

408
00:31:01,470 --> 00:31:03,000
He doesn't deserve to live!

409
00:31:04,780 --> 00:31:05,580
Get the hell up

410
00:31:05,870 --> 00:31:07,130
and hold the position!

411
00:31:07,340 --> 00:31:08,100
Or

412
00:31:08,190 --> 00:31:09,260
I'll have you court-martialed!

413
00:31:09,260 --> 00:31:10,060
Commander.

414
00:31:10,100 --> 00:31:11,360
We're so outnumbered.

415
00:31:11,470 --> 00:31:13,670
Are you sending our men to their deaths?

416
00:31:14,300 --> 00:31:16,430
I'll go find Commander Tang
for reinforcements.

417
00:31:16,430 --> 00:31:17,700
You hold the position here!

418
00:31:17,700 --> 00:31:19,150
Commander, but...

419
00:31:19,340 --> 00:31:20,340
Trust me!

420
00:31:21,710 --> 00:31:24,230
Guys, cover the Battalion Commander!

421
00:31:35,950 --> 00:31:37,060
Japs!

422
00:31:37,300 --> 00:31:37,990
Bring it on!

423
00:31:40,500 --> 00:31:42,710
He sold us all out.

424
00:31:42,710 --> 00:31:44,630
Do you still think he's a good guy?

425
00:31:47,710 --> 00:31:49,570
The Battalion Commander Du I know

426
00:31:50,320 --> 00:31:51,320
isn't like that.

427
00:32:02,590 --> 00:32:03,190
Go on.

428
00:32:04,260 --> 00:32:05,190
Get out of here

429
00:32:05,340 --> 00:32:06,230
and leave Nanjing.

430
00:32:06,230 --> 00:32:07,990
Three or four kilometers east
is the refugee camp.

431
00:32:07,990 --> 00:32:08,470
Go on!

432
00:32:08,470 --> 00:32:09,470
-Hurry up, hurry up.
-Move.

433
00:32:09,470 --> 00:32:10,150
Hurry up!

434
00:32:13,060 --> 00:32:14,190
Where are you going?

435
00:32:14,290 --> 00:32:15,150
I'm going back.

436
00:32:15,150 --> 00:32:16,260
We can't abandon our positions.

437
00:32:16,260 --> 00:32:17,300
Everyone knows

438
00:32:17,670 --> 00:32:18,890
Nanjing can't be held any longer.

439
00:32:18,890 --> 00:32:21,390
Even if we can't hold it,
we still have to defend it!

440
00:32:21,390 --> 00:32:23,100
If Nanjing falls, what's next?

441
00:32:23,100 --> 00:32:24,820
We'll have to fight for Hankou.
If Hankou falls,

442
00:32:24,820 --> 00:32:25,600
we'll have to fight for Chongqing.

443
00:32:25,600 --> 00:32:27,740
And if we don't hold Chongqing,
we'll have to keep retreating!

444
00:32:27,740 --> 00:32:29,020
If this continues, the entire country

445
00:32:29,020 --> 00:32:30,340
will fall into the hands of the Japanese!

446
00:32:30,340 --> 00:32:31,940
Where else can we retreat to?

447
00:32:58,780 --> 00:33:00,060
Rubbish!

448
00:33:01,300 --> 00:33:02,700
Still talking back, huh?

449
00:33:03,190 --> 00:33:04,100
Still trying to play tough, huh?

450
00:33:04,100 --> 00:33:04,710
Boss.

451
00:33:05,960 --> 00:33:08,160
Director Li is back and wants to see you.

452
00:33:13,350 --> 00:33:15,700
Qing, rip out all his fingernails.

453
00:33:15,910 --> 00:33:16,500
Yes, sir.

454
00:33:30,100 --> 00:33:31,340
If it weren't for saving you,

455
00:33:31,340 --> 00:33:32,610
he wouldn't have been taken away.

456
00:33:32,610 --> 00:33:33,580
And here you are, still playing

457
00:33:33,580 --> 00:33:36,310
that lousy three-stringed instrument
of yours.

458
00:33:38,260 --> 00:33:39,920
He still owes us a lot of money.

459
00:33:40,350 --> 00:33:41,820
Stop thinking about money.

460
00:33:41,820 --> 00:33:43,350
Saving him is what matters.

461
00:33:45,230 --> 00:33:46,540
If he isn't back

462
00:33:47,260 --> 00:33:48,540
within 3 days,

463
00:33:50,020 --> 00:33:51,280
then that's just fate.

464
00:33:52,820 --> 00:33:54,470
Well, I refuse to believe in fate.

465
00:33:54,470 --> 00:33:55,930
I'll find a way to save him.

466
00:33:55,950 --> 00:33:56,550
Director.

467
00:33:57,540 --> 00:33:58,780
When I went in,

468
00:33:58,910 --> 00:34:00,540
Chief Yu was already dead.

469
00:34:02,470 --> 00:34:03,430
Who killed him?

470
00:34:03,430 --> 00:34:04,150
No idea.

471
00:34:04,950 --> 00:34:06,210
Still investigating.

472
00:34:09,270 --> 00:34:10,530
If even you don't know,

473
00:34:11,540 --> 00:34:12,790
then nobody does.

474
00:34:15,580 --> 00:34:17,380
As long as Yu can't talk anymore,

475
00:34:18,350 --> 00:34:19,210
that's enough.

476
00:34:20,659 --> 00:34:22,100
As for Inspector Su,

477
00:34:22,699 --> 00:34:24,830
shouldn't we give her an explanation?

478
00:34:29,449 --> 00:34:31,380
Didn't you just arrest a young man?

479
00:34:31,620 --> 00:34:32,179
Yes.

480
00:34:33,100 --> 00:34:35,389
But I think besides him,

481
00:34:35,389 --> 00:34:36,310
there might be others...

482
00:34:36,310 --> 00:34:37,310
Let's go with him.

483
00:34:38,989 --> 00:34:40,100
We need to wrap this up

484
00:34:40,100 --> 00:34:41,310
as soon as possible

485
00:34:41,469 --> 00:34:43,330
to avoid further complications.

486
00:34:43,750 --> 00:34:44,480
Understood.

487
00:34:50,699 --> 00:34:51,989
You're framing me!

488
00:35:03,620 --> 00:35:04,310
Mr. Zhao.

489
00:35:06,140 --> 00:35:08,270
Is this the guy who killed Director Yu?

490
00:35:11,370 --> 00:35:12,780
[Confession]

491
00:35:12,910 --> 00:35:14,240
He doesn't look like it.

492
00:35:14,780 --> 00:35:15,610
Who cares?

493
00:35:19,060 --> 00:35:20,660
Now that Director Yu's out of the picture,

494
00:35:20,660 --> 00:35:24,060
you, Director Zhao, will be
sitting in that chair from now on.

495
00:35:24,060 --> 00:35:25,060
How great is that.

496
00:35:25,990 --> 00:35:27,720
That's not an easy seat to fill.

497
00:35:27,870 --> 00:35:28,670
Don't jinx me.

498
00:35:29,830 --> 00:35:32,230
What's Director Li
planning to do with him?

499
00:35:34,310 --> 00:35:36,370
Will Inspector Su go along with this?

500
00:35:36,790 --> 00:35:38,050
Dead men tell no tales.

501
00:35:38,390 --> 00:35:40,120
She'll have to go along with it.

502
00:35:48,540 --> 00:35:50,540
It wasn't Cang Guanglian who did it?

503
00:35:51,170 --> 00:35:52,500
I don't think it was him.

504
00:35:54,140 --> 00:35:56,100
Yu Yingxiang was strangled to death.

505
00:35:56,100 --> 00:35:57,220
I followed Cang Guanglian in—

506
00:35:57,220 --> 00:35:59,020
we were less than a minute apart.

507
00:35:59,140 --> 00:36:01,470
A person being strangled would struggle.

508
00:36:04,750 --> 00:36:06,140
So Yu Yingxiang was already dead

509
00:36:06,140 --> 00:36:07,940
before Cang Guanglian arrived.

510
00:36:12,750 --> 00:36:15,220
It seems Li Moqun had long since decided

511
00:36:15,220 --> 00:36:16,540
to silence him.

512
00:36:21,350 --> 00:36:23,750
Yu Yingxiang was Li Moqun's chief steward.

513
00:36:24,500 --> 00:36:26,960
He not only masterminded the assassination

514
00:36:27,020 --> 00:36:29,420
but likely committed other crimes as well.

515
00:36:30,050 --> 00:36:33,250
He knew all along that
you were following Cang Guanglian.

516
00:36:34,350 --> 00:36:36,140
Talk about feigning one thing

517
00:36:36,140 --> 00:36:37,340
while doing another.

518
00:36:38,830 --> 00:36:40,830
Cang Guanglian arrested a suspect,

519
00:36:40,830 --> 00:36:42,230
An acquaintance of ours.

520
00:36:42,990 --> 00:36:43,660
Who?

521
00:36:44,990 --> 00:36:45,720
Chen Kailai.

522
00:36:49,390 --> 00:36:51,190
What does he have to do with this?

523
00:36:51,640 --> 00:36:53,570
The bathhouse owner is his friend,

524
00:36:53,750 --> 00:36:55,950
and he was at the scene when it happened.

525
00:36:58,100 --> 00:36:59,960
That guy really has some bad luck.

526
00:37:00,700 --> 00:37:02,700
The murder was arranged by Li Moqun,

527
00:37:04,140 --> 00:37:05,140
but the poor guy

528
00:37:05,830 --> 00:37:07,290
ended up as the scapegoat.

529
00:37:08,270 --> 00:37:10,270
There was another face at the scene.

530
00:37:14,020 --> 00:37:14,750
Who?

531
00:37:37,470 --> 00:37:38,270
Inspector Su.

532
00:37:39,270 --> 00:37:40,310
Visiting so late—

533
00:37:41,310 --> 00:37:42,840
is there something urgent?

534
00:37:50,180 --> 00:37:51,440
You don't remember me?

535
00:37:54,860 --> 00:37:55,530
I do.

536
00:38:03,390 --> 00:38:04,790
Can you help me this once?

537
00:38:05,910 --> 00:38:06,620
How?

538
00:38:08,860 --> 00:38:10,720
Your boss, Yu Yingxiang, is dead.

539
00:38:12,500 --> 00:38:13,180
I'm aware.

540
00:38:13,620 --> 00:38:16,430
Did he usually like to go to Fairy Bath?

541
00:38:19,180 --> 00:38:21,640
How would I know
my superior's whereabouts?

542
00:38:22,020 --> 00:38:23,220
When he died,

543
00:38:24,700 --> 00:38:26,230
you were there at the scene.

544
00:38:32,220 --> 00:38:35,150
Inspector Su, you don't suspect
I killed him, do you?

545
00:38:43,140 --> 00:38:44,200
I went to take a bath

546
00:38:45,540 --> 00:38:47,940
and somehow turned myself
into a murderer?

547
00:38:49,100 --> 00:38:50,560
Murder requires a motive,

548
00:38:51,390 --> 00:38:52,190
Inspector Su.

549
00:38:57,750 --> 00:38:58,660
Do you have one?

550
00:39:03,790 --> 00:39:04,350
No.

551
00:39:06,060 --> 00:39:07,180
Li Moqun does.

552
00:39:07,700 --> 00:39:08,950
If Director Li were going to do it,

553
00:39:08,950 --> 00:39:10,010
he wouldn't use me.

554
00:39:11,060 --> 00:39:12,100
He has his own people.

555
00:39:12,100 --> 00:39:13,220
Who would he use?

556
00:39:14,220 --> 00:39:14,910
No idea.

557
00:39:21,100 --> 00:39:23,100
That photographer, Chen Kailai—

558
00:39:24,330 --> 00:39:25,530
does he have a motive?

559
00:39:28,790 --> 00:39:30,790
Chen Kailai has already confessed.

560
00:39:31,840 --> 00:39:32,760
Confessed?

561
00:39:35,750 --> 00:39:37,010
Is there any evidence?

562
00:39:38,700 --> 00:39:39,430
I don't know.

563
00:39:39,750 --> 00:39:41,480
You'd have to ask Captain Cang.

564
00:39:42,700 --> 00:39:45,500
And the execution should be carried out
very soon.

565
00:39:52,220 --> 00:39:53,150
You've changed,

566
00:39:54,430 --> 00:39:55,270
Mr. Zhao.

567
00:40:00,700 --> 00:40:01,470
So have you,

568
00:40:03,310 --> 00:40:04,110
Inspector Su.

569
00:40:11,830 --> 00:40:12,830
He's a decent guy.

570
00:40:15,910 --> 00:40:17,710
It'd be a shame if he really died.

571
00:40:34,830 --> 00:40:35,660
I'm leaving

572
00:40:37,100 --> 00:40:37,910
for France.

573
00:40:41,100 --> 00:40:42,560
How about giving me a gift?

574
00:40:44,340 --> 00:40:44,890
This.

575
00:41:12,830 --> 00:41:15,030
I'll return it to you when we meet again.

576
00:41:49,220 --> 00:41:50,620
You killed Yu Yingxiang.

577
00:41:54,910 --> 00:41:56,240
Who ordered you to do it?

578
00:41:58,140 --> 00:41:58,870
It wasn't me.

579
00:42:03,500 --> 00:42:05,230
Why were you at the crime scene?

580
00:42:08,390 --> 00:42:09,520
Who are you, anyway?

581
00:42:10,430 --> 00:42:11,950
I'm a photographer.

582
00:42:13,310 --> 00:42:14,390
I only take photos.

583
00:42:15,180 --> 00:42:16,310
I don't kill people.

584
00:42:27,310 --> 00:42:28,370
But you confessed.

585
00:42:31,910 --> 00:42:32,830
I didn't.

586
00:42:33,780 --> 00:42:36,710
You forced me to put my fingerprints
on the document.

587
00:42:50,270 --> 00:42:51,470
I didn't kill anyone.

588
00:42:54,060 --> 00:42:55,660
I didn't kill anyone!

589
00:42:57,620 --> 00:42:59,430
I didn't kill anyone!
